    "preamble": "Rajendra vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh Through ... on 24 July, 2017 1 M.Cr.C. No.7749/2017",
    "facts": "2. It is submitted by the petitioner that he is being prosecuted for the charge under Section 7/16 Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954. After completion of the prosecution evidence, at the stage of defence, the petitioner has filed an application under Section 243 readwith Section 293 of Cr.P.C. for calling the Public Analyst, State Food Laboratory, Bhopal and one Shailesh Gupta. The application was dismissed by the learned trial Court and learned Revisional Court has confirmed the order of trial Court. 3. It is submitted that two reports were filed by the prosecution before the trial Court to prove the adulteration but there is difference between both the reports about contemptuous substance. State Food Laboratory has found the sample according to the standards but the Central Food Laboratory found that the sample was of sub-standard. It is further submitted that he has challenged the process adopted by the Food Inspector while taking the sample. For these reason statement of the Public Analyst and the Panch witness - Shailesh Gupta were necessary to prove his defence. He filed an application for calling both of them as defence witness. 4. The application was dismissed by the trial Court considering the provisions of Section 13 (5) of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 and Section 4 of the Evidence Act which provides that the report of Central Food Laboratory supersedes report of State Food Laboratory, therefore, no useful purpose would be achieved by calling public analyst.",
